'pragmat'module=argnum,title="a number from the command line".
$ The rule 'arg number', copied into collatz, cal, sieve, bignum, queens
$ and life, as a module of its own (roman and caesar have variants).
$ To use it in a program, add 'pragmat'require="argnum". to it, comment
$ out the program's own 'arg number', and compile it together with argnum.
$ HEADER ******************************************************
$ convert the argument STDARG[ptr] to a positive number; fail if
$ it is not a sequence of digits
'q'arg number+>ptr+n>.

$ BODY ********************************************************
'pragmat'if=compile.
'q'arg number+>ptr+n>-i-c:
   0->n->i,string elem+STDARG+ptr+0+#,
   (nxt:string elem+STDARG+ptr+i+c,
          (=c= [/0/:/9/],subtr+c+/0/+c,addmult+n+10+c+n,incr+i,:nxt;
               -);
        +).
'root'+.
'pragmat'endif=compile.
'end'
